  "question": "The business requirements for the order processing system are described as follows: The enterprise has multiple customers, each with a customer ID, name, and contact information. The enterprise offers a variety of products, each with a product ID, product name, price, and inventory quantity. Customers can place orders, with each order having an order ID, product ID, customer ID who placed the order, order quantity, and order status. An order can include multiple products. For each order, a picking list is generated, which includes a picking list ID, order ID, product ID, picking quantity, and picking status. Based on the order and customer information, a delivery order is generated, which includes a delivery order ID, order ID, delivery time, and delivery status. Based on the order and customer information, a customer invoice is generated, which includes an invoice ID, order ID, invoice amount, and invoice date. Based on the customer and order information, an accounts receivable report is generated, which includes a report ID, order ID, receivable amount, and report date. The system ensures the entire process from customer order placement to product delivery and invoice generation is efficient and accurate through the collaborative work of multiple modules.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0467\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `products` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `orders` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  KEY `orders_ibfk_1` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `orders_ibfk_2` (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `orders_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `products` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `picking_lists` (\n  `picking_list_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `picking_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `picking_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`picking_list_id`),\n  KEY `picking_lists_ibfk_1` (`order_id`),\n  KEY `picking_lists_ibfk_2` (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `picking_lists_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `orders` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `picking_lists_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `products` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `delivery_orders` (\n  `delivery_order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `delivery_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`delivery_order_id`),\n  KEY `delivery_orders_ibfk_1` (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `delivery_orders_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `orders` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer_invoices` (\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `invoice_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `invoice_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invoice_id`),\n  KEY `customer_invoices_ibfk_1` (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_invoices_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `orders` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_receivable_reports` (\n  `report_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receivable_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `report_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_id`),\n  KEY `accounts_receivable_reports_ibfk_1` (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_receivable_reports_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `orders` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
